# =====================================================================
# Release V112 -- Rename Rebooked_Cancellations -> Cancellations_Rebooked + regenerate PBI views
# =====================================================================
# Renames the aggregate column to the preferred "Cancellations Rebooked" (Gold column
# Cancellations_Rebooked -> PBI view "Cancellations Rebooked"). Also REGENERATES the Gold->PBI
# views, which V111 did not do -- that is why the model/csx could not find the new column even
# though the Gold column existed. The csx measure "Cancellations Rebooked" (renamed from
# "Cancellation Rebook") + Config Display_Name are updated in the repo.
#
# MIGRATE drops the old column + adds the new (empty; repopulated on reload; must precede the SP
# redeploy). DEPLOY updates the aggregate load SP to the new name. EXEC regenerates the PBI views
# so [Aggregate Site Patient Practitioner Daily] exposes "Cancellations Rebooked".
#
# APPLY after deploy:
#   1. Reload the aggregate (Orchestrate_Build, or EXEC Gold.usp_Load_Aggregate_Site_Patient_Practitioner_Daily)
#      so Cancellations_Rebooked populates.
#   2. Refresh the model, THEN apply PBI_Dentally.csx (the [Cancellations Rebooked] column now resolves).
# Run: .\Scripts\Deploy.ps1 -Manifest Releases\V112__rename_cancellations_rebooked.manifest -SkipTests
# =====================================================================

MIGRATE  Migrations\V112__rename_cancellations_rebooked.sql
DEPLOY   Fabric\Gold.usp_Load_Aggregate_Site_Patient_Practitioner_Daily.StoredProcedure.sql
EXEC     EXEC Meta.usp_Create_Gold_Views;

TEST
